Original commit body from 37986ca3866085c67a254a293569350e05044ed0:

A catalogue row must name the boundary its call actually crosses.

- System.Exit exitWith / exitFailure / exitSuccess were env_write, which
  derives a host_env taint sink, so exiting read as writing the environment.
  They are declared not I/O (javascript.yaml's ruling for process.exit).
  die writes its message to stderr before exiting, so it moves to logging.
- Prelude.readIO was fs_read but parses a String the caller already holds;
  a must_not_exist fs_read claim was violated by a parse. Removed.
- System.Info os / arch / compilerName / compilerVersion were
  host_info_read but are fixed when GHC is built. Removed. As values they
  were never applied, so the row was also unreachable.

System.Exit and System.Info gain module_completeness grants recording the
ruling, so a qualified call into either is an examined negative rather than
an unexamined module.

Tested at the finding level (ADR-0049 ruling 3): verify-claims over a
program that only parses and exits no longer returns violated for the
env_write and fs_read claims, and each removal is paired with a control in
the same block (setEnv, readFile, readLn, getProgName) that still classifies.

Addresses INV-dozuj, INV-savuk, INV-banid.

